ration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T12:43:44Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Are these military call signs?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T12:43:50Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Cooper", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T12:43:54Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "DB Cooper", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T12:44:07Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "Answer: DB COOPER", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T12:44:16Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "5. The Fugitive Earl\nIn the dark hours of November 7th, 1974, a London nanny was brutally murdered in a basement, and a terrifying struggle left a noblewoman covered in blood. The prime suspect was her estranged husband, a high-stakes gambler who fled into the night and left his car abandoned at a coastal port. Though sightings of him have been reported from the jungles of Africa to the outback of Australia, the British aristocracy’s most famous fugitive was never seen again. What was the title of this infamous man, the 7th Earl of his name?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]